# What each surface is drawn from, for `shots` without surfaces: a change renders the surfaces of
# the lines that list its most specific match. One per line, `SURFACE PATH...`, a path being a file
# or a folder; SURFACE may join several with `+`. The groups:
#
# - `*` is everything: the tokens and their generator, the lockfiles that pin every build, and
#   the harness. A path under one of its paths is listed nowhere else, or a change there would
#   render less than everything.
# - `shell` is every shell surface (`scenarios`), `specimen` every page of the specimen, `iced`
#   every page of kubaos-specimen's (all but `specimen/qml`), `mockups` every page of the mockup
#   site (design/mockups).
#
# The other shared inputs render the surfaces that build against them. The QML components:
# the shell and qml-specimen. kubaos-ui's code and kubaos-geometry: the iced renderers, Kōbō and
# kubaos-specimen. Its fonts: those, the shell and qml-specimen (their fontconfig), and the
# terminals (kubaos-tokens sizes them by Geist Mono). Its symbols: those but the terminals
# (kubaos-tokens writes the QML symbols from them). The boot screens and the pointer read none.
#
# Every surface has a line of its own (`test/shots/shots-test` checks it): the shell's, kobo,
# terminals (test/shots/terminals), plymouth, grub and cursor (test/shots/boot), and the
# specimen's pages, `specimen/PAGE` for kubaos-specimen's and `specimen/qml` for qml-specimen's, and
# the mockups' pages, `mockups/PAGE` for `design/mockups/src/pages/LEVEL/PAGE.ts`.
# The shell's services are stand-ins (fakes/qs/services): of config/quickshell/services, only the
# JavaScript the stand-ins load is drawn. The specimen's `pages/icons.rs` is in `specimen`: every
# page loads its fonts.
